.\" kld.1 — manual for the kldload operator console hub. mdoc, OpenBSD
.\" section order. Keep in lockstep with the --help banner in main.go.
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt KLD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kld
.Nd the kldload operator console, in a terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar section
.Nm
.Fl -tui
.Op Ar section
.Nm
.Ar section
.Fl -print
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the kldload operator console as one program for a desktop and a headless
box alike.
Under a display
.Pq Ev DISPLAY No or Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
it opens the web console in a standalone app window through
.Xr kldload-chrome-app 1 ,
so a window manager and a browser see the same console;
without one, or with
.Fl -tui ,
it is a terminal program with the eight sections of that console:
Overview, Machines, Storage, Network, Cluster, Metrics, Estate and Provision.
Each section is read from the tool that owns the fact and shown as it is:
.Xr kldload-estate 8
for the machines and the drift,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8
for the host's health,
.Xr zpool 8
and
.Xr kldload-rollback 8
for storage and boot environments,
.Xr wg 8
for the mesh,
.Xr kubectl 1
for the cluster after a port probe of the apiserver, the Prometheus targets
API for metrics, and
.Xr kldload-netboot-server 8
for the rack.
.Pp
.Nm
is a hub, not another console.
The deep views stay in
.Xr vmxplore 1 ,
.Xr zxplore 1 ,
.Xr wgx 1
and
.Xr k9s 1 ;
.Nm
opens the one that belongs to the current section on
.Ic Enter
and returns when it exits.
Its verbs run the shipped commands
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-snap 8
and
.Xr kvm-delete 8 ,
never a re-implementation of them, so what the terminal does is what the
estate tests prove.
.Pp
With a
.Ar section
argument the console opens on that section.
With
.Fl -print
it renders that section once to standard output, without a terminal, and
exits; the text is the same the console shows.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar section
One of
.Cm overview , machines , storage , network , cluster , metrics , estate
or
.Cm provision ,
case-insensitive.
.It Fl -tui
The terminal console even under a display.
.It Fl -print
Render the named section once and exit.
Useful from scripts and over an ssh command that has no terminal.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and the build stamp.
.It Fl h , -help
Print the usage and the key map, and exit 0.
.El
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "Shift-Tab" -compact
.It Ic 1 No to Ic 8
Switch to that section.
.It Ic Tab , Shift-Tab
Next and previous section.
.It Ic j , k
Move the selection down and up.
.It Ic r
Reload the section.
.It Ic Enter
Open the section's deep console
.Pq Xr vmxplore 1 , Xr zxplore 1 , Xr wgx 1 , Xr k9s 1 .
.It Ic c
Clone the selected machine
.Pq Xr kvm-clone 8 ;
asks for the new name.
.It Ic s
Snapshot the selected machine
.Pq Xr kvm-snap 8 .
.It Ic d
Delete the selected machine and its zvol
.Pq Xr kvm-delete 8 Fl -force ;
asks for the machine's name to be typed, and does nothing otherwise.
.It Ic a
In Provision, arm a machine for a netboot install
.Pq Xr kldload-netboot-server 8 Cm arm-install ;
asks for the MAC (or
.Cm any
for open mode) and the answers file.
.It Ic x
In Provision, disarm the selected machine
.Pq Xr kldload-netboot-server 8 Cm disarm .
.It Ic \&?
Show the key map.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
The exit status is 2 for a section that does not exist.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Open the console on the machines:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kld machines
.Ed
.Pp
Print the estate's drift and the doctor's findings from a script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kld estate --print
42 machines across leases, libvirt, state_db, wireguard; 1 drift; doctor 22 ok 1 warn 1 fail 18 skip
machine               finding        detail                                            repair
klab-green-fedora     unregistered   libvirt knows this domain; the state DB does not  kldload-db vm-register --name klab-green-fedora --role <class>
.Ed
.Pp
Ask which build is installed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kld --version
kld 0.1.0 b3af6a94
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A section whose tool did not answer shows the tool's own error in red where
the table would be, and the rest of the console keeps working; for example
.Dq apiserver https://10.251.0.1:6443 does not answer (port probe)
in Cluster on a host whose kubeconfig points at a cluster that is gone.
A verb that fails shows the failing command and its message on the status
line; nothing is retried.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vmxplore 1 ,
.Xr wgx 1 ,
.Xr zxplore 1 ,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kldload-estate 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-delete 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in kldload 1.6 (September 2026), when the four terminal consoles had
four key maps and the first answers an operator wants lived in eight
different commands.
.Sh CAVEATS
Every collector elevates with
.Xr sudo 8
.Fl n ;
a user without passwordless sudo sees each section's error instead of its
table.
The Cluster section needs a kubeconfig on the host; a hypervisor that is not
a cluster node says so rather than showing an empty table.
